sched-walt (soc-repo): build on the 6.18 scheduler and binder

sched-walt.ko is a load dependency of ufs-qcom (sched_set_boost,
walt_{,un}set_enforce_high_irq_cpus), msm_performance, thermal_pause, bwmon and qcom_lpm.
All 58 vendor hooks it registers still exist in ACK 6.18 and are still called (hook audit in
bsp618/PORT-STATUS.md); two changed:

- android_vh_binder_restore_priority lost its task argument: both remaining call sites passed
  current on 6.12, so the hook uses current.
- binder_transaction.need_reply is gone: it was set for exactly the synchronous non-reply
  transactions, i.e. !is_reply && !is_async.

Scheduler internals:
- pick_task(rq) -> pick_task(rq, rf); it may return RETRY_TASK (sched_ext balance only):
  the CPU drain loop (core_ctl halt) picks again.
- set_next_entity() gained `bool first` (the extern is unused; prototype fixed).
- cfs_rq.h_nr_running -> h_nr_queued is done by the port618.py rule cfs-h-nr-queued.

Per-task data guard: WALT stores struct walt_task_struct (456 bytes on 6.18) right after
task_struct; the area exists only with the boot argument android_arch_task_struct_size=512.
Without it walt_init() corrupted every neighbouring task_struct on 6.12 (ab-s60..s62). The
module now checks ksize(current) at load and stays inert (no hooks, no walt_init) with a
pr_crit instead.

--- a/bsp612/soc-repo/kernel/sched/walt/walt.c
